In this discussion, James presented a table of results comparing two methods, focusing on countries that experienced sign changes in their outputs. I recommended highlighting significant countries based on global salience and magnitude of changes, including populous nations like Pakistan (sign flip from negative to positive), and Canada (major positive to negative flip). Other notable mentions included Ukraine, Uzbekistan, and Netherlands, considering their geopolitical relevance. For smaller than average nations, I suggested mentioning Kyrgyzstan and Romania due to their substantial sign change magnitudes. Ultimately, I provided a compact shortlist for inclusion in James’s work, emphasizing both impactful sign changes and demographic significance to underline the relevance of the findings in global sustainability dialogues.
